    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d361">

                <pb facs="0416" n="366" xml:id="pg366"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Baron Fava.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-12-10"><hi rendition="#italic">December 10,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 27th ultimo, and to inform you in reply that
                    inasmuch as it appears from the statements therein contained that the
                    importation of salt into Sicily and Sardinia is not prohibited, and that salt
                    imported from the United States is admitted free of duty, the collectors of
                    customs at the principal ports of the United States were, on the 7th instant,
                    instructed to admit salt imported from those islands to entry free of duty.</p>
                <p>Accept, Mr. Ambassador, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
